error: Missing #[capsule(...)] attribute

       The ComputationalCapsule derive macro requires capsule configuration.

       Add this attribute to your struct:
       #[capsule(alignment = 64)]

       Common configurations:
       - alignment = 64:  Standard single cache line (most common)
       - alignment = 128: Dual cache line (DualAtomicU64 pattern)
       - alignment = 256: Multi-line capsules (large state)

       Optional parameters:
       - size = N:    Expected struct size in bytes
       - tier = "T":  Capsule tier (Atomic, SIMD, FixedPoint, etc.)
       - auto_pad = true: Generate padding suggestion

       Example:
       #[derive(ComputationalCapsule)]
       #[capsule(alignment = 64, size = 64)]
       #[repr(C, align(64))]
       struct MyCapsule { ... }

       Help: Add #[capsule(alignment = 64)] before your struct
